{"id":"lane-saatchi-review","parent":"saatchi-v1","ord":"a2","title":"review: claude-opus","done":"2026-08-28T15:39:38-04:00","after":["lane-saatchi-refactor"],"created":"2026-08-28T14:56:26-04:00","changed":"2026-08-28T15:39:44-04:00","custom":{"reviewer":"agent-claude-opus","terminal":"7459a3a5","verdict":"HOLD — 2 MUST, 4 SHOULD, 5 NIT; the shape and the hard parts endorsed (group teardown \"the correct design\", the leak fix narrow, portability clean, CI honest). MUST 1: the try starts after import/read/launch, so a broken evidence.ts — the likeliest consumer failure — dies as a raw stack with no saatchi: line and a misattributed app.log tail. MUST 2: video mode never drains ffmpeg's stderr pipe (hang on long recordings) and a failed transcode still prints shot→mp4 and exits 0 with zero artifacts. SHOULDs: HUP missing from the trap (app survives holding the port); README's flake block is the spec's not the repo's (the #417 class); example shots tracked yet gitignored — fresh cannot clean them; the 30s readiness budget undocumented and pre-spent by cold builds. NITs incl. ${self} vs untracked lib files, unanchored shot() regex, stdin/SIGTTIN, args silently ignored, darwin declared never run. PR comment 5456966639."}}
