{"id":"saatchi-publish","parent":"saatchi-root","ord":"a1","title":"saatchi#publish: the shots leave the machine","doing":true,"desc":"The second flake app, ruled with the human 2026-08-28: `nix run github:juspay/saatchi#publish` — no arguments — uploads .saatchi/shots/ to GitHub's user-attachments endpoint (repo from gh repo view, auth from gh auth token, webm transcoded, failures named) and prints one paste-ready markdown block to stdout. The default app untouched. GitHub-only by ruling (\"we can always add bitbucket support in future\"). Same PR, the human's ruling: README reworked for its two readers — a human learning what saatchi is, an agent operating it autonomously from the repo alone — with the repo-layout section cut. Dogfood: the olai#419 lane publishes its evidence through this branch onto the real PR.\n\n**MERGE AUTHORIZATION STANDING** (the human, 2026-08-28 ~16:25, question tool): approval given with the ruling \"after dogfood+review\" — once the review round folds and the dogfood lands clean, the orchestrator merges WITHOUT a further ask.","created":"2026-08-28T16:10:41-04:00","changed":"2026-08-28T16:25:25-04:00","custom":{"agent":"agent-pi","brief":"briefs/saatchi-publish.md","dispatched":"2026-08-28T16:22:00-04:00","merge":"merge-human","pr-url":"https://github.com/juspay/saatchi/pull/2","terminal":"417828a1","tier":"ordinary","worktree":".worktrees/publish"}}
